# 2026-09-13 (gen514) — full live KB; development probes, never persisted training.
# The pieces found by triaging the 33 open questions of the r300 prose ladder.
# Sentences are from that ladder or describe mechanics; no world fact of the
# ladder is stored in the KB.

[test the bare verb of an object question reaches a curated inflected relation]
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/profiles/agi.p0
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset
!timeout 60
> A coral reef is an underwater ecosystem. Coral belongs to the class Anthozoa in the animal phylum Cnidaria, which includes sea anemones and jellyfish.
<~ includes sea anemones
# «include» is the stem of the curated `includes`, and it closes the phrase
# («the phylum cnidaria», not «phylum_cnidaria_include»).
> what does the phylum cnidaria include?
<~ sea anemones

[test a bare plural describes the specific entity]
!reset
!timeout 30
> Shallow coral reefs occupy less than 0.1% of the world's ocean area.
<~ Learned
> what do reefs occupy?
<~ ocean area

[test a spoken construction can swap the roles]
!reset
!timeout 30
> Coral reefs are under threat from excess nutrients.
# 2026-09-18: «threat from excess» was read by the event reader (E3) as an
# event with an origin — «Noted: The threat is from excess.» — and the prose
# fact was lost. A bare «from» is not an event.
<! Noted
<~ Learned
> what threatens coral reefs?
<~ excess nutrients

[test a participle before «from» is not an event with an origin]
!reset
!timeout 60
> Most coral reefs are built from stony corals, whose polyps cluster in groups.
<! Noted
<! is from
> what are most coral reefs built from?
<~ stony corals
> what kind of corals are most reefs built from?
<~ stony

[test a percentage without its connector is not a computation]
!reset
!timeout 30
> Reefs have declined by 50% since 1950.
<! 975
> what is 15% of 80?
<~ 12

[test the perfect is not possession]
!reset
!timeout 30
> Reefs have declined.
<! Learned
> what have reefs declined by?
<! Reefs
> Zelnik has a handle.
<~ Learned
> does zelnik have a handle?
<~ Yes

[test a piece of a phrase is not the thing asked]
!reset
!timeout 30
# The live KB holds provides(ocean, water): the question is about ocean waters.
> what do those ocean waters provide?
<! dissolved oxygen
> what does the ocean provide?
<~ water

[test a whole-part relation keeps its direction]
!reset
!timeout 30
> Reefs are formed of colonies of coral polyps held together by calcium carbonate.
<~ Learned
> what are reefs made of?
<~ colonies
# It answered «Reefs.»: colonies made of reefs is the opposite of the text.
> what are colonies made of?
<! Reefs
> what is made of colonies?
<~ Reefs
# The direction is taught knowledge: retract it and the old guess comes back.
> forget that "made of" is a whole-part relation
<~ no longer
> what are colonies made of?
<~ Reefs
> "made of" is a whole-part relation
<~ Learned
> what are colonies made of?
<! Reefs

[test most attenuates a generalization, several stays refused]
!reset
!timeout 30
> Most coral reefs are built from stony corals.
<~ Learned
> what are most coral reefs built from?
<~ stony corals
!query attenuated_reading(most, $S)
> Several pilots are sailors.
<~ can't hold

[test a possessive relative speaks of the possessed noun]
!reset
!timeout 60
> A coral reef is an underwater ecosystem. Coral reefs are built from stony corals, whose polyps cluster in groups.
<~ polyps of stony corals
> where do the polyps of stony corals cluster?
<~ groups

[test a verb adverb is not an object]
!reset
!timeout 30
> Most reefs grow best in warm water.
<! grow best
> where do most reefs grow best?
<~ warm

[test where are and at what ask the place, with the type checked]
!reset
!timeout 60
> Coral reefs flourish in ocean waters. They are most commonly found at shallow depths in tropical waters, but deep water coral reefs exist in other areas.
<~ located in shallow depths
> where are coral reefs most commonly found?
<~ shallow depths
> at what depths are reefs commonly found?
<~ shallow depths
> at what time are reefs found?
<! shallow depths

[test a relative with bare that and coordinated predicates]
!reset
!timeout 60
> A coral reef is an underwater ecosystem. Unlike sea anemones, corals secrete hard carbonate exoskeletons that support and protect the coral.
<~ protect coral
> what supports the corals?
<~ exoskeletons
> what protects the corals?
<~ exoskeletons
> what do corals secrete?
<~ exoskeletons

[test examples introduced by including do not steal the main clause]
!reset
!timeout 90
> Coral reefs occupy less than 0.1% of the ocean. Yet, they provide a home for at least 25% of all marine species, including fish, mollusks, worms and sponges.
<~ at least 25 percent of all marine species live in
> what do coral reefs provide a home for?
<~ marine species
> how many marine species do reefs provide a home for?
<~ 25
> what lives in coral reefs?
<~ marine species

[test what is X says what was read, and only about X]
!reset
!timeout 90
> A coral reef is an underwater ecosystem characterized by reef-building corals. Most coral reefs are built from stony corals, whose polyps cluster in groups.
<~ Learned
> what are stony corals?
<~ I read
> what is a reef?
<~ underwater ecosystem
> what kind of ecosystem is a coral reef?
<~ underwater
> what is the annual global economic value of coral reefs?
<! I read
> what is a compass used for?
<~ finding north

[test a copula-led construction is asked without its copula]
!reset
!timeout 30
> Coral reefs are under threat from excess nutrients.
<~ Learned
> what are coral reefs under threat from?
<~ excess nutrients

[test a fronted participle speaks of the main subject]
!reset
!timeout 60
> A coral reef is an underwater ecosystem. Sometimes called rainforests of the sea, shallow coral reefs form some of Earth's most diverse ecosystems.
<~ rainforests of the sea
> what are shallow coral reefs sometimes called?
<~ rainforests of the sea

[test a trailing because, two particles, and an adjective relation]
!reset
!timeout 60
> Coral reefs flourish in ocean waters. Shallow tropical coral reefs have declined by 50% since 1950, partly because they are sensitive to water conditions.
<~ declined since 1950
> what have shallow tropical coral reefs declined by?
<~ 50 percent
> since when have coral reefs declined?
<~ 1950
> what are coral reefs sensitive to?
<~ water conditions

[test a parenthetical gives the examples of the phrase before it]
!reset
!timeout 60
> Coral reefs flourish in ocean waters. They are under threat from excess nutrients (nitrogen and phosphorus), rising ocean heat content and acidification.
<~ includes nitrogen
> what do excess nutrients include?
<~ nitrogen
> what threatens coral reefs?
<~ excess nutrients

[test the type decides between two descriptions]
!reset
!timeout 90
> Reefs are formed of colonies of coral polyps held together by calcium carbonate. Most coral reefs are built from stony corals, whose polyps cluster in groups.
<~ Learned
> what kind of corals are most reefs built from?
<~ stony corals
> what holds coral polyps together?
<~ calcium carbonate
> what is calcium carbonate for?
<~ holding colonies of coral polyps together

[test the value of an attribute, and what was estimated]
!reset
!timeout 90
> Coral reefs deliver ecosystem services for tourism, fisheries, and shoreline protection. The annual global economic value of coral reefs has been estimated at anywhere from US$30–375 billion (1997 and 2003 estimates) to US$2.7 trillion (a 2020 estimate).
<~ estimated at
> what is the annual global economic value of coral reefs?
<~ billion
> what has been estimated at billions?
<~ economic value
> what do coral reefs deliver services for?
<~ tourism

[test a rank inside a rank, and an agentive compound]
!reset
!timeout 90
> A coral reef is an underwater ecosystem characterized by reef-building corals. Coral belongs to the class Anthozoa in the animal phylum Cnidaria, which includes sea anemones and jellyfish.
<~ class anthozoa belong
> what phylum does coral belong to?
<~ cnidaria
> what class does coral belong to?
<~ anthozoa
> what do reef-building corals build?
<~ reefs

[test a partitive of is not a particle, and the chain needs an asked type]
!reset
!timeout 90
> Reefs are formed of colonies of coral polyps. Sometimes called rainforests of the sea, shallow coral reefs form some of Earth's most diverse ecosystems. Coral belongs to the class Anthozoa in the animal phylum Cnidaria.
<~ Learned
> what are reefs formed of?
<! ecosystems
> what do shallow coral reefs form?
<~ diverse ecosystems
> what does coral belong to?
<~ anthozoa
